WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.313
You checked every prevention setting
and every rule on a test device.

3
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.624
You triggered Microsoft Learn's
network protection test.

4
00:00:08.624 --> 00:00:11.236
You filed the fleet's
audit and block events,

5
00:00:11.236 --> 00:00:14.138
and its Attack Surface
Reduction events by rule.

6
00:00:14.138 --> 00:00:18.825
And you stepped one rule back on one
device, the way the guide's rollback does.

7
00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:22.722
The evidence an I S S O keeps
from this module: the antivirus,

8
00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:27.349
firewall and Attack Surface Reduction
policy exports for each ring;

9
00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:30.110
the weekly audit and block query results;

10
00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:34.737
the network protection test and the
tamper status; the per-rule tests;

11
00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:38.796
the rule-by-ring matrix, with
the date each rule entered block;

12
00:00:38.796 --> 00:00:42.125
and every exclusion, with
its approver and expiry.

13
00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:45.033
Next is Module 3, exposure and incidents,

14
00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:51.170
where every vulnerability gets an owner
and every incident gets triaged to a table.
